{"url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/jcc/education/postgraduate-programmes/interdisciplinary-phd-programme-in-veterinary-medicine", "final_url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/jcc/education/postgraduate-programmes/interdisciplinary-phd-programme-in-veterinary-medicine", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-18", "text": "Home\nAbout Us\nEducation\nResearch\nServices\nDonations\nNews and Events\nJCC e-shop\nIntranet\nEducation Postgraduate Programmes Interdisciplinary PhD Programme in Veterinary Medicine\nInterdisciplinary PhD Programme in Veterinary Medicine\nCity University of Hong Kong (CityUHK) is a dynamic, fast-growing university that is pursuing excellence in research and professional education. As a publicly-funded institution, the University is committed to nurturing and developing students\u2019 talents and creating applicable knowledge to support social and economic advancement.\nThe Jockey Club College of Veterinary Medicine and Life Sciences (JCC) was established in collaboration with Cornell University\u2019s College of Veterinary Medicine. The JCC is the first and only veterinary school in Hong Kong and is envisioned as a centre of excellence in animal health education, research and discovery, and clinical care in China and the Asia-Pacific region.\nProgramme Overview\nThe Interdisciplinary PhD Programme in Veterinary Medicine (VM/P) is open to outstanding graduate students who wish to conduct state-of-the-art basic, clinical and translational life sciences research alongside research professionals. The students will participate in research programmes leading to PhD degrees in one of the following areas and will be jointly supervised by a faculty advisor from CityUHK and a faculty advisor from Cornell University.\nComparative Biomedical Sciences\nImmunology and Infectious Disease\nMolecular and Systemic Neuroscience\nPublic Health and Epidemiology\nThe programme is student-centred and led by faculty who are accessible, engaged and committed to ensuring that our postgraduate students reach their full potential in research, teaching and professional development. In addition, students will be provided the unique opportunity with financial sponsorship to conduct research work at the Cornell University co-supervisor\u2019s laboratory at Ithaca, New York, for a period of 3 to 12 months during their senior years of studies.\nPROGRAMME\nInterdisciplinary PhD Programme in Veterinary Medicine\nAWARD TITLE\nGraduates will be awarded the degree of \u201cDoctor of Philosophy\u201d of the City University of Hong Kong\nPROGRAMME CODE\nVM/P\nMEDIUM OF INSTRUCTION AND ASSESSMENT\nEnglish\nNORMAL STUDY PERIOD\nFull-time: 4 year\nFINANCIAL AID & FEES\nPlease refer to SGS website\nPOGRAMME COORDINATOR\nProf. Paulo STEAGALL\nFUNDING\nSelf-financed (institutional-funded)\nStudentships Award\nCurriculum Information Record (CIR)\nUseful Information\nAdmission\nWe invite applications from qualified candidates with a bachelor degree or higher in all areas of life sciences and medicine, with preference given to graduates with training in veterinary medicine. Prospective students are encouraged to make contact with faculty members of JCC or the Department of Biomedical Sciences and Department of Neuroscience to discuss the proposed research project before application. Profiles of the faculty members can be found in the department websites below:\nDepartment of Infectious Diseases and Public Health\nDepartment of Veterinary Clinical Sciences\nDepartment of Biomedical Sciences (Under College of Biomedicine)\nDepartment of Neuroscience (Under College of Biomedicine)\nPlease submit an application online (https://www.cityu.edu.hk/pg/research-degree-programmes/apply-now) in order to receive full consideration. Applications are accepted all year round and will be considered altogether in early December of each year for the September intake of the subsequent year.\nThe entire application package should include the supporting documents listed on the admission application checklist and should be uploaded to the admission system by early December for consideration. The Admission Committee will take into account the following factors in making admission decisions: academic excellence; research integrity, ability and potential; communication and interpersonal skills; and leadership abilities.\nContact Us\nVM/P Programme Office\njcc.vmp@cityu.edu.hk\nMonday to Friday: 09:00-12:30, 14:00-17:50\nSaturday, Sunday and Public Holidays: Closed\n10/F, Jockey Club One Health Tower\nCity University of Hong Kong\nTat Chee Avenue, Kowloon\nHong Kong\nAbout Us\nThe College\nOur People\nDepartments\nCollege Brochure\nDiversity, Equity and Inclusion\nCollege Excellence Awards\nContact Us\nEducation\nBachelor of Veterinary Medicine\nPostgraduate Programmes\nResearch\nCentre for Applied One Health Research and Policy Advice\nCentre for Animal Health and Welfare\nDepartment of Infectious Diseases and Public Health\nServices\nAffiliated CityU Subsidiaries\nContinuing Professional Education\nDonations\nDonations\nLittle Angel Educational Memorial Programme\nNews and Events\nJCC Newsletter\nNews\nEvents\nCritters\nJCC e-shop\nIntranet\nStaff Intranet\nStudent Intranet\nPrivacy Policy\nCopyright\nDisclaimer\nAccessibility\nWe use cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website.\nMore Information\nConfirm", "links": [["", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc"], ["Jockey Club College of Veterinary Medicine and Life Sciences", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc"], ["Home", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc"], ["About Us", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc/about-us"], ["Overview", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc/about-us"], ["The College", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc/about-us/the-college"], ["Overview", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc/about-us/the-college"], ["Dean's Welcome", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc/about-us/the-college/deans-welcome"], ["Vision & Mission", "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/jcc/about-us/the-coll